-- חוזר לבעלויות תש"ע/1: ביצוע פסק דין של בית הדין הארצי לעבודה בעניין
-- הפרשות לקרנות פנסיה עבור עובדי הוראה
-- Carrying out the National Labour Court's ruling on pension contributions
-- for teaching staff employed by the owners of secondary schools: the new
-- contribution rates from 30.11.09, the 1% salary addition, the compensation
-- for over-deduction with interest and linkage, and the veteran-fund rates.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תש"ע/1 ביצוע פסק דין בעניין הפרשות לקרנות פנסיה`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date (22.11.2009), addressee, greeting and subject line, which names the Treasury letter of 18/11/09 the instructions follow and says bracketed remarks are the Ministry's; no rule.

-- Time in this file is counted in DAYS from 22 November 2009, the date the
-- circular is signed (day 0).
`30 November 2009` MEANS 8

@desc The kind of pension fund a teaching employee is insured in.
DECLARE `pension fund kind` IS ONE OF
    `a new pension fund`
    @desc a veteran fund to which chapter ז1 of the Financial Services Supervision (Insurance) Law, 1981 applies
    `a veteran pension fund`

@desc Contribution rates as fractions of the salary they are taken on.
DECLARE `contribution rates` HAS
    `employer contribution rate`           IS A NUMBER
    `employee deduction rate`              IS A NUMBER

@desc A teaching employee of the owner of a secondary school, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `pension employee` HAS
    `employed by the owner of a secondary school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed by an owning body (בעלות) of a secondary (על-יסודי) school
    `fund kind`                           IS A `pension fund kind`
    `pensionable salary`                  IS A NUMBER @desc the monthly pensionable salary (שכר פנסיוני), shekels
    `gross salary`                        IS A NUMBER @desc the monthly gross salary (שכר ברוטו), shekels
    `over-deducted months`                IS A LIST OF `over-deducted month`

@desc One month between 1.1.04 and 30.11.09 in which contributions were made at 12% employer and 5.5% employee.
DECLARE `over-deducted month` HAS
    `pensionable salary that month`       IS A NUMBER @desc the pensionable salary in the month the contribution was made
    `months from contribution to payment` IS A NUMBER @desc whole months from the contribution to the day the compensation is paid
    `index known at the contribution`     IS A NUMBER @desc the consumer price index known at the contribution (section 3(ג)(3))
    `index known at the payment`          IS A NUMBER @desc the consumer price index known on the day the compensation is paid
    `employer rate that month`            IS A NUMBER
    `employee rate that month`            IS A NUMBER
    `day of the contribution`             IS A NUMBER @desc days from 22 November 2009 (negative before it)

DECLARE `pension action` IS ONE OF
    `contribute and deduct` HAS `employer contribution paid` IS A NUMBER
                                `employee deduction made`    IS A NUMBER
    `pay the 1% addition` HAS `addition paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the compensation` HAS `compensation paid` IS A NUMBER
    `transfer additional budget for the compensation`

§§ `1 הרקע לפסק הדין`

-- akn:art_1 The background: the rates customary until the ruling (13.5% employer, 4% employee), their conflict with the Income Tax (Provident Funds) Regulations, the 2003 events, and the 12% / 5.5% rates many owners moved to; narrative, no rule. Section 3(ג) uses the 12% / 5.5% rates as its condition.

`the rates customary before the ruling` MEANS `contribution rates` 0.135 0.04
`the rates many owners moved to` MEANS `contribution rates` 0.12 0.055

§§ `2 פסק הדין של בית הדין הארצי לעבודה`

-- akn:art_2/p1 The ruling's guiding principle, quoted: teachers do not lose and employers do not gain, the employers' cost and the teachers' income unchanged; the rulings follow. The principle is checked in the worked examples against section 3's instructions.

@desc The salary a percentage is taken of.
DECLARE `salary base` IS ONE OF
    `the gross salary`
    `the pensionable salary`

-- Section 2 restates what the court ruled; section 3 instructs. The ruling
-- is encoded as data so that section 3 can be checked against it.
-- Section 2(א): for teachers insured in new pension funds, 12.5% employer
-- (1% less than before) and 5% employee (1% more), from two months after
-- the ruling, that is from 30.11.09.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
`the rates the ruling sets for new funds` MEANS `contribution rates` 0.125 0.05
`the day the ruling's rates begin` MEANS `30 November 2009`

-- Section 2(ב): teachers insured in the new funds are entitled to an
-- addition of 1% of their GROSS salary (a "refund" of the extra 1%
-- deducted), from two months after the ruling (F-2009-10_tasha_01-a).
@ref akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_b
GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1% addition as the ruling states it` e IS
    IF `entitled to the 1% addition` e
    THEN e's `gross salary` TIMES 0.01
    ELSE 0

`the base the ruling gives the 1% addition` MEANS `the gross salary`

-- Section 2(ג): teachers in the new funds from whom 12% / 5.5% were
-- contributed while the case ran are compensated for the over-deduction at
-- 1.5% for the whole period, within two months of the ruling, with interest
-- and linkage; section 3(ג) carries it out.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_c
`the compensation rate the ruling sets` MEANS 0.015

-- Section 2(ד): for teachers in veteran funds the old rates plus 1.5% on
-- each side, as the law on the veteran funds' recovery sets, are lawful
-- and stay: 15% employer and 5.5% employee.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_d
`the rates the ruling keeps for veteran funds` MEANS `contribution rates` 0.15 0.055

§§ `3 הנחיות לביצוע פסק הדין`

-- akn:art_3/p1 The lead-in to the instructions; no rule of its own.

GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this circular applies to` e IF
    e's `employed by the owner of a secondary school`

§§§ `3(א)`

-- Section 3(א): from 30.11.09, for teachers employed by the owners of
-- secondary schools insured in a new fund, 12.5% employer (6.5% severance,
-- 6% benefits) and 5% employee (benefits); 3(ד): in a veteran fund under
-- chapter ז1 of the Financial Services Supervision (Insurance) Law, 15%
-- (13.5% + 1.5%) employer and 5.5% (4% + 1.5%) employee. In both, no change
-- in the salary components contributions are made on: the base is the
-- pensionable salary as it was. No deadline is printed for a month's
-- contribution, so the duty has none.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a akn:art_3__para_d
GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pension action`
DECIDE `the month's contribution` e IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `contribute and deduct` `employer part` `employee part`
          PROVIDED     `employer part` EQUALS e's `pensionable salary` TIMES (`the contribution rates from 30.11.09` (e's `fund kind`))'s `employer contribution rate`
                   AND `employee part` EQUALS e's `pensionable salary` TIMES (`the contribution rates from 30.11.09` (e's `fund kind`))'s `employee deduction rate`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "sections 3(א) and 3(ד): contributions at the rates from 30.11.09"

GIVEN k IS A `pension fund kind`
GIVETH A `contribution rates`
DECIDE `the contribution rates from 30.11.09` k IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a new pension fund` THEN `contribution rates` 0.125 0.05
    WHEN `a veteran pension fund` THEN `contribution rates` 0.15 0.055

@desc The share of the employer's 12.5% that goes to severance pay (פיצויים); the rest is benefits (תגמולים).
`the severance part of the employer's contribution` MEANS 0.065
`the benefits part of the employer's contribution` MEANS 0.06

§§§ `3(ב)`

-- Section 3(ב): from 30.11.09 a teacher employed by the owner of a
-- secondary school and insured in a new fund is entitled to an addition of
-- 1% of the PENSIONABLE salary. Section 2(ב) says the court gave 1% of the
-- GROSS salary (F-2009-10_tasha_01-a); the instruction is encoded as
-- written. No deadline is printed for paying it, so the duty has none.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b
GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 1% addition` e IS
    IF `entitled to the 1% addition` e
    THEN e's `pensionable salary` TIMES 0.01
    ELSE 0

GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the 1% addition` e IF
        `this circular applies to` e
    AND e's `fund kind` EQUALS `a new pension fund`

`the base section 3(ב) gives the 1% addition` MEANS `the pensionable salary`

GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pension action`
DECIDE `paying the 1% addition` e IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay the 1% addition` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the 1% addition` e
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 3(ב): the 1% addition from 30.11.09"

-- Section 3(ב), second paragraph: the addition is a separate line on the
-- payslip; it counts toward the minimum-wage top-up, payment for paid
-- absence and severance pay under the Severance Pay Law; it is not in the
-- base of percentage additions or of the hourly value, and no contributions
-- are made on it.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b/p2
GIVEN u IS A `salary use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1% addition counts toward` u IF
    CONSIDER u
    WHEN `the minimum-wage top-up` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `payment for paid absence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `severance pay under the Severance Pay Law` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@desc What a salary payment may be counted toward.
DECLARE `salary use` IS ONE OF
    `the minimum-wage top-up`
    `payment for paid absence`
    `severance pay under the Severance Pay Law`
    `the base of percentage additions`
    `the hourly value`
    `pension and other contributions`

@ref akn:art_3__para_b/p2
`the payslip line the 1% addition is shown on` MEANS `a separate line`

DECLARE `payslip line` IS ONE OF
    `a separate line`
    `merged into another line`

§§§ `3(ג)`

-- Section 3(ג)(1): a teacher employed by the owner of a secondary school,
-- insured in a new fund, for whom 12% / 5.5% were contributed in all or
-- part of 1.1.04–30.11.09, is compensated with 1.5% of the pensionable
-- salary of each such month, by its value that month, with interest and
-- linkage from the contribution to the payment. The table of coefficients
-- the paragraph says is attached is not in the document (a corpus defect:
-- only its title, "טבלת מקדמים", is printed), so the coefficients are
-- computed from the rate and the index.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c__subpara_1
GIVEN m IS AN `over-deducted month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `compensation for the month` m IS
    IF      `a month that earns compensation` m
        AND m's `day of the contribution` AT LEAST `1 January 2004`
        AND m's `day of the contribution` AT MOST `30 November 2009`
    THEN m's `pensionable salary that month`
         TIMES `the compensation rate`
         TIMES `linkage factor` m
         TIMES `interest factor for` (m's `months from contribution to payment`)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN m IS AN `over-deducted month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a month that earns compensation` m IF
        m's `employer rate that month` EQUALS 0.12
    AND m's `employee rate that month` EQUALS 0.055

`the compensation rate` MEANS 0.015

-- 1 January 2004 as a day number counted from 22 November 2009.
`1 January 2004` MEANS -2152

@export The compensation for over-deduction a teaching employee insured in a new pension fund is owed under circular תש"ע/1, section 3(ג)
GIVEN e IS A `pension employee` @desc the employee and the months in which 12% / 5.5% were contributed
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the compensation` e IS
    IF      `this circular applies to` e
        AND e's `fund kind` EQUALS `a new pension fund`
    THEN sum (map `compensation for the month` (e's `over-deducted months`))
    ELSE 0

-- The paragraph's own note: no additional budget goes to the owners for
-- these contributions, the Ministry's budgeting in those years having
-- included 13.5%. No time limit is printed.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c__subpara_1/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pension action`
DECIDE `no additional budget for the compensation` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    SHANT `transfer additional budget for the compensation`
    LEST BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "section 3(ג)(1): no additional budget is transferred for the compensation"

-- Section 3(ג)(2): the effective interest is 2.25% for twelve months, or
-- 0.1855% a month. "Effective" interest is compounded; the monthly figure
-- is applied month by month.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c__subpara_2
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `interest factor for` n IS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN 1
    ELSE (1 PLUS `the monthly interest rate`) TIMES `interest factor for` (n MINUS 1)

`the monthly interest rate` MEANS 0.001855
`the yearly interest rate` MEANS 0.0225

-- Section 3(ג)(3): linkage by the known consumer price index the Central
-- Bureau of Statistics publishes.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c__subpara_3
GIVEN m IS AN `over-deducted month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `linkage factor` m IS
    m's `index known at the payment` DIVIDED BY m's `index known at the contribution`

-- Section 3(ג)(4): the compensation is paid to the teacher no later than
-- 30.11.09. Section 2(ג) gives the same deadline: two months from the
-- ruling, which section 2(א) dates as 30.11.09.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c__subpara_4
GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pension action`
DECIDE `paying the compensation` e IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay the compensation` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the compensation` e
    WITHIN `30 November 2009`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 3(ג)(4): the compensation is paid no later than 30.11.09"

-- Section 3(ג)(5): the compensation is not counted for the hourly value
-- and no contributions are made on it.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c__subpara_5
GIVEN u IS A `salary use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the compensation is excluded from` u IF
    CONSIDER u
    WHEN `the hourly value` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `pension and other contributions` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- akn:art_4 The contact line for questions and the title of the attached table of coefficients ("חוזר תש"ע – טבלת מקדמים"), whose rows the document does not carry; no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

`the two parts make the employer's 12.5%` MEANS
    `the severance part of the employer's contribution` PLUS `the benefits part of the employer's contribution`
    EQUALS (`the contribution rates from 30.11.09` `a new pension fund`)'s `employer contribution rate`
#ASSERT `the two parts make the employer's 12.5%`

-- Section 3 carries out section 2's rates as ruled.
#ASSERT `the contribution rates from 30.11.09` `a new pension fund` EQUALS `the rates the ruling sets for new funds`
#ASSERT `the contribution rates from 30.11.09` `a veteran pension fund` EQUALS `the rates the ruling keeps for veteran funds`
#ASSERT `the compensation rate` EQUALS `the compensation rate the ruling sets`

-- Section 3(ד): 15% = 13.5% + 1.5% and 5.5% = 4% + 1.5%, as printed.
#ASSERT (`the contribution rates from 30.11.09` `a veteran pension fund`)'s `employer contribution rate` EQUALS 0.135 PLUS 0.015
#ASSERT (`the contribution rates from 30.11.09` `a veteran pension fund`)'s `employee deduction rate` EQUALS 0.04 PLUS 0.015

-- F-2009-10_tasha_01-a: the ruling as section 2(ב) states it and the
-- instruction of section 3(ב) take the 1% on different salaries.
`the ruling and the instruction take the 1% addition on different salaries` MEANS
    NOT (`the base the ruling gives the 1% addition` EQUALS `the base section 3(ב) gives the 1% addition`)
#ASSERT `the ruling and the instruction take the 1% addition on different salaries`

-- Section 2's principle: the employer's cost and the teacher's net are
-- unchanged. Under section 3(ב)'s base it holds; the old rates were 13.5% / 4%.
GIVEN e IS A `pension employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer's cost is unchanged for` e IF
    e's `pensionable salary` TIMES 0.135
    EQUALS e's `pensionable salary` TIMES 0.125 PLUS `the 1% addition` e

-- Section 3(ג)(2)'s two figures state one rate: 0.1855% is the monthly
-- equivalent of 2.25% a year rounded to four digits, and twelve of it
-- compound to 2.2489%, within two thousandths of a percentage point. This
-- file applies the monthly figure, the one stated per month as the
-- compensation is.
#ASSERT `the yearly interest rate` MINUS (`interest factor for` 12 MINUS 1) AT MOST 0.00002
#ASSERT `the yearly interest rate` MINUS (`interest factor for` 12 MINUS 1) AT LEAST 0

-- The salaries and index values are round placeholders.
`a new-fund teacher` MEANS
    `pension employee` WITH
        `employed by the owner of a secondary school` IS TRUE
        `fund kind`            IS `a new pension fund`
        `pensionable salary`   IS 8000
        `gross salary`         IS 10000
        `over-deducted months` IS LIST `over-deducted month` 6000 12 100 100 0.12 0.055 (0 MINUS 365),
                                       `over-deducted month` 6000 0 100 100 0.135 0.04 (0 MINUS 30)

#ASSERT `the 1% addition` `a new-fund teacher` EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `the 1% addition as the ruling states it` `a new-fund teacher` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the employer's cost is unchanged for` `a new-fund teacher`
#EVAL   `the compensation` `a new-fund teacher`
#ASSERT `the compensation` `a new-fund teacher` EQUALS 90 TIMES `interest factor for` 12

#TRACE `paying the compensation` `a new-fund teacher` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the compensation` 92.03 AT 5
#TRACE `paying the compensation` `a new-fund teacher` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the compensation` 92.03 AT 20
#TRACE `the month's contribution` `a new-fund teacher` AT 8 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `contribute and deduct` 1000 400 AT 30
